.TH RUSTYBATTERY 1 "November 2026" "RustyBattery 0.11.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rustybattery, battery \- Per-app power tracker, battery optimizer, and Smart Saver for Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B battery
[\fB\-\-summary\fR]
[\fICOMMAND\fR]
.br
.B rustybattery
[\fB\-\-summary\fR]
[\fICOMMAND\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B RustyBattery
is a lightweight, zero-dependency Linux battery & per-app power monitor written in Rust.
It tracks per-application energy drain (\fB%\fR, \fBFocused %\fR, \fBWh\fR, \fBW\fR),
Screen-On Time (\fBSoT\fR), Sleep/Suspend drain (\fB%/hr\fR), and battery health in a local
SQLite database, and provides both an interactive terminal UI and a 24/7 systemd user daemon.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B (no command)
Launch the interactive TUI dashboard.
.TP
.B summary [\-\-hours N] [\-\-top N] [\-\-json]
Print a CLI power summary, Screen-On Time, Sleep/Suspend drain, and top draining apps.
Pass \fB\-\-hours 0\fR (default) for since last full charge, or \fB\-\-json\fR for JSON output.
.TP
.B optimize [\-\-dry\-run]
Scan and interactively optimize background hogs and system power tunables.
.TP
.B sleep [\-\-fix]
Audit \fBs2idle\fR sleep mode, lid state, noisy ACPI USB/PCI wakeup triggers, Bluetooth status,
and 24h sleep drain rate. Pass \fB\-\-fix\fR to immediately apply \fBs2idle\fR optimizations.
.TP
.B autopilot [status|on|off|whitelist APP|unwhitelist APP|config]
View or configure Smart Battery Saver rules, thresholds, and protected app whitelist.
.TP
.B freeze APP \fR/\fB resume [APP | \-\-all] \fR/\fB stop APP
Freeze (\fBcgroup.freeze = 1\fR or \fBSIGSTOP\fR), resume (pass \fB\-\-all\fR to thaw all frozen user cgroups), or gracefully stop a running application.
.TP
.B doctor
Inspect cgroup v2 availability, active window focus method, RAPL access, power-profile backend, charge limits, and database health.
.TP
.B service [install|uninstall|status]
Manage the 24/7 systemd user background collector (\fBrustybattery.service\fR).
.TP
.B statusbar [\-\-format waybar|polybar|i3|plain] [\-\-top N] [\-\-print\-config]
Output compact JSON/text status for Waybar, Polybar, or i3status.
.TP
.B notify
Send a desktop notification with current battery status and top draining apps.
.TP
.B man [\-\-install]
Open this manual page in \fBman\fR, or install \fBrustybattery.1\fR and \fBbattery.1\fR into
\fI~/.local/share/man/man1/\fR so \fBman battery\fR and \fBman rustybattery\fR work directly.
.SH TUI KEYBOARD & MOUSE CONTROLS
.TP
.B ↑ / ↓ \fRor\fB j / k
Move app selection (or scroll wheel). Left-click selects a row; right-click opens details.
.TP
.B Enter / d
Open or close the \fBApp Battery Details\fR inspector modal.
.TP
.B /
Live-filter applications by name or category (\fBEnter\fR applies, \fBEsc\fR clears).
.TP
.B Tab / 1\-4
Switch time range: \fB1\fR Since Full Charge, \fB2\fR 6h, \fB3\fR 24h, \fB4\fR 7d (or click tabs).
.TP
.B s / f
Cycle sort column (\fBs\fR) or category filter (\fBf\fR: All / User Apps / System).
.TP
.B c
Toggle charts visibility (Auto / Show / Hide).
.TP
.B o
Open the interactive \fBBattery Optimizer\fR modal.
.TP
.B a / A
Toggle Smart Battery Saver (\fBa\fR) or open the live \fBSmart Saver Rules & Log\fR editor (\fBShift+A\fR).
.TP
.B z / w / x
On the selected app: freeze/resume (\fBz\fR), toggle Smart Saver whitelist (\fBw\fR), or stop (\fBx\fR).
.TP
.B q
Quit the TUI.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/rustybattery/config.toml
Persistent Smart Battery Saver rules, thresholds, and protected app whitelist.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/rustybattery/history.db
SQLite database storing battery samples, Screen-On Time, and per-app energy buckets.
.TP
.I ~/.config/systemd/user/rustybattery.service
Systemd user unit for the 24/7 background collector and Smart Saver daemon.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B battery
Open the interactive TUI.
.TP
.B battery summary \-\-hours 24 \-\-top 10
Show 24-hour SoT, sleep drain, and top 10 draining apps.
.TP
.B battery autopilot whitelist Spotify
Protect Spotify from being auto-frozen by Smart Saver.
.TP
.B battery man \-\-install
Install \fBman battery\fR and \fBman rustybattery\fR locally.
